-- title:
--   Tangent coordinates of an affine combination of two endomorphisms
-- statement:
--   Let $T'$ be an Artinian local ring with residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,T'$, let $I \subseteq T'$ be an ideal contained in the maximal ideal with $I\cdot\mathfrak m = 0$, and let $V$ be a finite-dimensional $k$-vector space (with the matching right action and central scalars) which is also a $T'$-module compatibly with the $k$-action, together with an injective $T'$-linear map $\iota : V \to T'$ whose range is $I$ viewed as a $T'$-submodule. Let $C$ be a flat $T'$-algebra, $q_Y : Y \to \operatorname{Spec} T'$ a scheme over $T'$ and $u : \operatorname{Spec} C \to Y$ a morphism over $\operatorname{Spec} T'$. Let $x_k : A_k \to \operatorname{Spec} k$ carry a relative group law $L_k$ (functorial multiplication, unit and inverse on $T$-points over $k$, with associativity, unit and inverse axioms and compatibility with base change), let $a_k : A_k \to Y$ exhibit $A_k$ as the fibre product of $q_Y$ with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue map, and let $U_e \subseteq A_k$ be an affine open through which the unit of $L_k$ factors via $e_1$. Let $r \in k$ be the residue of $a_r \in T'$, and let $\psi, \psi', \psi'' : C \to C$ be $T'$-algebra endomorphisms such that $\psi$ and $\psi'$ are congruent to the identity modulo the ideal generated by $I$ in $C$, and $\psi''(x) = \psi(x) + a_r\,(\psi'(x) - x)$ for all $x \in C$. Finally let $c, c' : \Gamma(A_k, U_e) \to \operatorname{Hom}_k(V^\vee, k \otimes_{T'} C)$ be tangent coordinate functions for the pairs $(u, u \circ \operatorname{Spec}\psi)$ and $(u, u \circ \operatorname{Spec}\psi')$ in the sense of `IsTangentCoordsOfPairAt`: for each of them there are a morphism $w_0$ from the spectrum of the thickening $(k \otimes_{T'} C) \otimes_k (k \oplus V)$ (trivial square-zero extension) to $A_k$ lying over the canonical base morphism, and a lift $w_1$ of the $L_k$-translate of $w_0$ through the open immersion $U_e \hookrightarrow A_k$, such that $w_0$ followed by $a_k$ is a tangent vector of the given pair (it factors, through a Schlessinger map on the pair ring of $I$ and $C$, over a morphism from the spectrum of that pair ring to $Y$ whose two restrictions are the two members of the pair), and the coordinate function is obtained by applying `tangentCoords` to the ring homomorphism induced by $w_1$ on $\Gamma(A_k, U_e)$. Then $c + r \cdot c'$ is a tangent coordinate function, in the same sense, for the pair $(u, u \circ \operatorname{Spec}\psi'')$.
--
--   This is the coordinate computation underlying the $k$-linearity of the Kodaira–Spencer type map attached to a small extension: it says that forming the affine combination $\psi + a_r(\psi' - \mathrm{id})$ of two endomorphisms congruent to the identity modulo $IC$ adds the corresponding tangent coordinates with the scalar $r$. It feeds the shift computation [`GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.isShiftBy_add_smul_of_isRegluingBy_of_isTangentCoordsOfPairAt_add_smul`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.isShiftBy_add_smul_of_isRegluingBy_of_isTangentCoordsOfPairAt_add_smul).
